\section{Gaussian kernel sums from flash attention}\label{sec:method}

Softmax attention is denoted by $\att_\tau(q,k,v)$ and given for $m=1,\ldots, M$ via
\begin{equation}\label{eq:att}
\att_\tau(q,k,v)_m\coloneqq\frac{\sum_{n=1}^N \e^{\tau q_m^\top k_n}v_n}{\sum_{n=1}^N \e^{\tau q_m^\top k_n}} \in\R^C ,
  \qquad
  \lse_\tau(q,k)_m \coloneqq \log \sum_{n=1}^N \e^{\tau q_m^\top k_n} \in \R.
\end{equation}
\texttt{Flash} attention evaluates \eqref{eq:att} with $\mathcal O(MN(D{+}C))$ operations and $\mathcal O((M{+}N)(D{+}C))$ memory.
The logits $\lse_\tau$ are computed as a by-product in $\mathtt{fp32}$, but no gradient is implemented.
To connect \eqref{eq:att} with Gaussian kernel sums, we first remove the normalization by multiplying with $\exp(\lse_\tau(q,k)_m)$ to get
\begin{equation}\label{eq:InterEq}

\begin{equation}\label{eq:InterEq}
   \textstyle  \sum_{n=1}^N \e^{\tau q_m^\top k_n} v_n = \att_\tau(q,k,v)_m \cdot \e^{\lse_\tau(q,k)_m}.
\end{equation}
Then, we introduce $\tilde v=(v_n \e^{-\frac{\tau}{2}\|k_n\|^2})_{n=1}^N$ to obtain
\begin{equation}
\frac{\att_\tau(q,k,\tilde v)_m \e^{\lse_\tau(q,k)_m}}{ \e^{\frac{\tau}{2}\|q_m\|^2}}
= \sum_{n=1}^N \e^{\tau q_m^\top k_n} v_n \e^{-\frac{\tau}{2}\|k_n\|^2} \e^{-\frac{\tau}{2}\|q_m\|^2} 
= \sum_{n=1}^N \Phi_\tau(q_m, k_n) v_n.
\end{equation}
Algorithm \ref{alg:lse_prescale} summarizes this method.
Unfortunately, this implementation cannot handle gradients.
